    "acceptanceCriteria": [
      {
        "id": "AC-1",
        "text": "A handler's `res.status(201).header(\"X-A\", \"1\").send(\"ok\")` reaches the client as status `201`, header `X-A: 1` and body `ok` with the `Content-Length` the core set; a `res.stream` response of unknown length arrives with an intact body and without a `Content-Length` and `Transfer-Encoding` conflict (chunked framing is asserted only for a body larger than the container's output buffer or after a flush, because a container may buffer a small body and frame it with a length); and no error page of the container appears for a `404` or `500` the core produced, because `sendError` is never called. [D-360]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 436
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-2",
        "text": "A HEAD request to a GET route returns the `Content-Length` of the GET body and no body bytes, and a `204` and a `304` carry no body, on the embedded container. [D-360; FR-HTTP-017]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 437
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-3",
        "text": "After `abort()` the next body write, `commit` or `finish` throws `IOException` (a write already blocked inside the container ends only by the container's write timeout, FR-SVL-006 AC-3), `abort()` called twice is harmless and `abort()` may run on another thread than the writer; a second `commit`, `sendFile` or `eventStream` on one exchange throws `IllegalStateException`. [r2 W2-006]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 438
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-4",
        "text": "`res.file` and `res.download` on a file serve the whole file, a single `Range` (`206` with `Content-Range`) and a `416`, byte for byte equal to the in-memory adapter, with `sendFile` copying in chunks of at most 64 KiB, which a spy output stream records, and never reading the file into memory; the class references no `java.nio.file` type. [D-360; FR-STATIC-010]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 439
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-5",
        "text": "Response header order on the wire is the container's, `docs/api/servlet.md` says so, and no test of the shared case suite depends on header order. [r2 W2-006]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 440
      }
    ],
